# Milestone: v0.10.10-job-introspection
# Covers: scopeTag with explicit tag label kills ',' strands when function
#         exits; without scopeTag the comma strand outlives the function call.
# blocked: T39 chk driver + OGET dispatch for native closures (v1.x bridge)
# matrix-row: tag-scopetag
#
# Reason:
#   scopeTag() shipped v0.10.10 (D7-D). Same blocker as scope-tag.chk:
#   the fixture uses legacy bare-name `var t = scopeTag;` which requires
#   the OGET dispatch path to wrap native closures as auto-invoked getters
#   (defers v1.x; workspace-root design-risks v0.10.10-A). The fixture
#   also requires `,` separator for the absence-of-scopeTag variant and
#   multi-second observation — both T39 chk driver. Single-strand cousin
#   `scope_tag_basic.chk` activates at v0.10.10.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate when T39 chk driver + native-closure OGET land):
# # function f() { { var t = scopeTag; t: { sleep(2s); echo("foo") }, echo("bar"); sleep(1s); echo("baz") }; sleep(2s); echo("xyzzy") } | f();
# # [00000001] *** bar
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/scope-tag2.chk)
